#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD2259 expect=noViolation domain=TS
#note "All INDIC rows pair TSVALCD and TSVAL from the same dummy-SNOMED concept (25064002=Headache, 422587007=Nausea), in the preferred case that the flag-less rule compares verbatim (D-TA-3 default, Fix #266; since the C1 data repair the pairs decodes carry the levels' preferred form, so the same TSVAL satisfies the membership twin FDA-SD2257/FDA-SD2267 as well); blank-code and blank-term INDIC rows do not fire (completeness is another rule's concern) and the mismatched pair on the AGEMAX row is outside the INDIC condition."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#dictionaries dummy
dataset TS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col TSSEQ    type=Num
col TSPARMCD type=Char
col TSVAL    type=Char
col TSVALCD  type=Char
---
S01 | TS | 1 | INDIC  | Headache | 25064002
S01 | TS | 2 | INDIC  | Nausea   | 422587007
S01 | TS | 3 | INDIC  | Headache |
S01 | TS | 4 | INDIC  |          | 422587007
S01 | TS | 5 | AGEMAX | Headache | 422587007
